    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section" id="page-mapping">
    <h2>7. Intended page mapping</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>View A:</strong> Homepage compact, How It Works, Canonical Workflow, Healthcare, Financial Services, Use Cases, Controlled Evaluation transaction summary.</li>
      <li><strong>View B:</strong> Platform, executive architecture, company overview where appropriate, pitch-deck architecture summary. Not automatic detailed deployment topology.</li>
      <li><strong>View C:</strong> Verification, Proof and Evidence, Compliance and Audit, Reviewer Kit, Sample Decision Record, Trust Center evidence summary where appropriate.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section" id="technical-classes">
    <h2>8. Separate technical diagram classes</h2>
    <p>
      These classes are not replaced automatically by Views A, B, or C in Pass 01B.
      Later passes will inherit the unified tokens, typography, connector weights,
      boundary treatments, iconography, and semantic path colors:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>DFD and Threat Flow</li>
      <li>Threat Model</li>
      <li>Deployment and Integration</li>
      <li>Enforcement Runtime</li>
      <li>Fail-Closed Security Gate</li>
      <li>Release Lifecycle</li>
      <li>Responsibility Matrix</li>
      <li>Record Anatomy</li>
      <li>Review Authorization Flow</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section" id="limitations">
    <h2>9. Known limitations</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Views A–C are not deployed across all 27 public routes in this pass.</li>
      <li>Homepage and Verification use deliberately simplified interim visuals.</li>
      <li>View C is illustrative and must not be mistaken for a live product screenshot.</li>
      <li>View B must not be interpreted as physical host, region, or air-gap separation.</li>
      <li>Existing Pass 01A dense diagrams remain on some pages until a later adoption pass.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section" id="approval-boundary">
    <h2>10. Approval boundary</h2>
    <p>
      All three views are required specialized architecture views. No universal
      winner was selected. No site-wide diagram deployment was performed in Pass
      01B. Pass 01C / Pass 02 adoption is not authorized by this validation alone.
      Merge to main requires Rodney’s explicit approval.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
